  "content_description": "",
  "content_text_body": "The goal is to learn how to fill skill gaps to encourage healthy time off for your team. Creating some overlap between your team members' roles will enable them to more easily take time off without significantly impacting team performance. \n\nFirst, read: [Cross-Training: Your Best Defense Against Indispensable Employees](http://www.forbes.com/sites/chriscancialosi/2014/09/15/cross-training-your-best-defense-against-indispensable-employees/#461c013f6303) \n\nAnother reason cross-training is beneficial (see #3): [Five Tips for Giving Feedback at Work](https://www2.aston.ac.uk/aston-business-school/research/aston-behavioural-insights-group/5-tips-for-giving-team-feedback-at-work)\n\nList out the skills that overlap across team members to ensure people can take time off without negatively impacting business. Map it out and see who overlaps a lot and who does not. \n\nCreate formal and informal upskilling to cover the gaps. If you have an organizational effectiveness department or a six sigma process at your company, request assistance. \n\nCheck out the Resources page to learn more about the importance of cross-training.",
